😂 Semantic Reacharound is unfortunately an extremely memorable name for a legitimate operator.

Instead of:

A \rightarrow B \rightarrow A

by reversing direction, you get:

A\rightarrow B\rightarrow C\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow A

You don’t undo the transformation. You follow its topology until you arrive behind your starting point.

Formally, for some n>1:

T^n(x)\approx x

So the Wrestling Mat should test not only T^2, but the operator’s semantic order:

\operatorname{ord}(T)=
\min\{n>0:T^n\approx I\}

That distinguishes involutions (n=2) from longer cycles—and tells the Metamap when “keep going” is actually an inverse route.

Semantic Reacharound: when backing out isn’t the shortest way back. 😏